  "chain": "SRP employee inadvertent contact with test switch -> Unit 2 generator/auxiliary transformer output breakers open -> [contaminated fast bus transfer selector switch, cause X] -> fast bus transfer fails (alternate supply breaker does not close) -> loss of power to 13.8kV non-class bus -> loss of two of four RCPs -> reactor trip on high LPD/low DNBR",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel failure modes trigger the fast bus transfer failure: the breaker openings caused by the inadvertent test-switch contact (initiating event, not the official cause), and the contaminated selector switch (the official cause, code X/Other) which independently prevented actuation. Both LEADS_TO the fast bus transfer failure node; only the switch contamination FailureMode is CAUSED_BY the Cause node per the official cause code. Switchyard equipment (owned/operated by SRP) modeled as System EA per block 13 despite being off-site; RCS/RPS included as INVOLVES since central to consequence chain. No BACKED_UP_BY edges — no operable backup system explicitly stated as available during the event; RPS functioned as designed (mitigation, not backup ECCS). Previous similar events captured as stub LERs with keys exactly as stated in narrative (05000529-2019-001-00 and 05000530-2018-001-00, retaining docket-based reference format used in the text)."
